  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Gaussian Mixture Models (EM)** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_gmm(X: list, k: int = 2, max_iter: int = 10) -> dict:\n    x = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64)\n    N, D = x.shape\n    means, vars_, weights = x[:k].copy(), np.ones((k, D)), np.ones(k) / k\n    for _ in range(int(max_iter)):\n        lik = np.zeros((N, k))\n        for j in range(k):\n            v = np.maximum(vars_[j], 1e-6)\n            lik[:, j] = weights[j] * np.exp(-0.5*np.sum(((x - means[j])**2)/v, axis=1)) / (np.sqrt((2*np.pi)**D * np.prod(v)) + 1e-12)\n        gamma = lik / (np.sum(lik, axis=1, keepdims=True) + 1e-12)\n        Nk = np.sum(gamma, axis=0) + 1e-12\n        weights = Nk / N\n        for j in range(k):\n            means[j] = np.sum(gamma[:, j:j+1]*x, axis=0) / Nk[j]\n            vars_[j] = np.maximum(np.sum(gamma[:, j:j+1]*((x - means[j])**2), axis=0) / Nk[j], 1e-6)\n    return {'means': np.round(means, 4).tolist(), 'variances': np.round(vars_, 4).tolist(), 'weights': np.round(weights, 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
